=== PARITY (vs web VersionInfoWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (VersionInfoSource → VersionInfoModel):
    useVersionInfo (/system/version), useCaptureStats, useTranslation. The web component reads its
    fields DEFENSIVELY off a loosely-typed record — chart_version/go_version/os/arch are strict in the
    DTO, while build_date/git_commit/uptime + the capture counters (signals_per_sec/messages_today/
    bytes_processed/avg_processing_latency_ms) are read with `(data as { … }).field` and fall back to
    '—' / 0. The native DTOs mirror this exactly (optional fields, em-dash / zero fallback). The view
    performs NO HTTP.
  Projection → VersionInfoProjection.vitals is a 1:1 port of the web body: chartVersion/goVersion/
    buildDate/uptime/os/arch = field ?? '—' (blank/whitespace treated as absent), truncatedSha =
    gitSha?.slice(0,7) ?? '—', capture counters ?? 0. kvItems = the five web rows (Version[bold] /
    Build Date / Git SHA[mono] / Go Version / Uptime). statItems = two tiles always (Signals/sec,
    Messages Today) + Bytes Processed + Avg Latency when isWide (web `if (isWide) items.push`).
    formatBytes ported: B (fmtInt) → KB/MB (1dp) → GB (2dp). Verified by an EXECUTED harness (54/54).
  Composition → glass shell (info.circle icon + "Version Info" title [hidden when compact] + freshness
    chip + refresh + optional Open) · compact layout (chartVersion bold + truncatedSha Badge, centered)
    · standard layout (KVList over the bottom-pinned 2-up stat grid) · wide layout (+ "OS: … • Arch: …"
    line + 4-up stat grid).
  Shared components → maps web @/components/data-display + @/components/feedback + @/components/ui to
    native: KVList→VersionInfoKVRow, Badge→VersionInfoBadge, StatCard(WidgetStatGrid)→
    VersionInfoStatTile, EmptyState→ContentUnavailableView, DataFreshness→VersionInfoFreshnessChip,
